Problem Statement

1. Title

Fleet Maintenance Scheduling Platform

---

2. Domain

Fleet Management / Transportation Technology / Smart Mobility

---

3. Who is the User?

Fleet Manager

Manages the organization's vehicles, monitors their maintenance requirements, schedules preventive maintenance and tracks the overall maintenance status of the fleet.

Maintenance Officer

Views assigned maintenance tasks, checks vehicle maintenance requirements, records service activities and updates maintenance status.

Administrator

Manages users, vehicles, maintenance categories and monitors the overall fleet maintenance system.

---

4. What Problem Are We Solving?

Organizations that operate multiple vehicles often depend on manual records, spreadsheets or separate systems to manage vehicle maintenance. As the number of vehicles increases, it becomes difficult to accurately track service schedules, maintenance history, mileage and upcoming maintenance requirements.

For example, a company may operate a fleet of 50 delivery vehicles. Each vehicle may have different service intervals based on its mileage, previous maintenance and vehicle type. If these details are maintained manually, a maintenance schedule can easily be missed. Delayed maintenance can increase the possibility of vehicle breakdowns, unexpected repair expenses, vehicle downtime and disruption to daily operations.

There is also often no centralized system that allows fleet managers and maintenance staff to easily view the current maintenance status of every vehicle.

The Fleet Maintenance Scheduling Platform aims to solve this problem by providing a centralized application for managing vehicles, scheduling preventive maintenance, tracking service history and monitoring upcoming and overdue maintenance.

---

5. Proposed Solution

The application will provide a centralized platform that helps organizations efficiently manage fleet vehicles and their maintenance activities.

The system will store vehicle information, maintenance records and service schedules in a centralized database. Fleet managers can schedule maintenance based on service dates or mileage intervals, while maintenance officers can view assigned tasks and update their completion status.

The system will also provide dashboards and notifications to help users identify upcoming and overdue maintenance.

