6. Core Entities / Database Tables

The initial system will contain the following core database entities:

1. User
2. Role
3. Vehicle
4. VehicleType
5. Maintenance
6. MaintenanceType
7. MaintenanceSchedule
8. MaintenanceAssignment
9. MaintenanceHistory
10. Notification

Main Relationships

User → Role

A user has a specific role such as Fleet Manager, Maintenance Officer or Administrator.

Vehicle → VehicleType

Each vehicle belongs to a particular vehicle type.

Vehicle → Maintenance

A vehicle can have multiple maintenance records.

Vehicle → MaintenanceSchedule

Each vehicle can have one or more scheduled maintenance activities.

Maintenance → MaintenanceType

Each maintenance activity belongs to a particular maintenance type such as oil service, brake inspection or general service.

Maintenance → MaintenanceAssignment

Maintenance tasks can be assigned to maintenance officers.

Maintenance → MaintenanceHistory

Completed maintenance activities are stored as historical records.

User → Notification

Users can receive notifications about upcoming or overdue maintenance.

