8. Success Criteria

The project will be considered successful when:

- A user can securely register and log in to the application.
- A Fleet Manager can add and manage vehicles.
- The system can store vehicle information in the database.
- A Fleet Manager can schedule maintenance for a vehicle.
- Maintenance can be scheduled based on date or mileage.
- The system can identify upcoming maintenance.
- The system can identify overdue maintenance.
- Maintenance Officers can view their assigned tasks.
- Maintenance Officers can update maintenance status.
- Completed maintenance can be recorded and stored as history.
- Users can view the complete maintenance history of a vehicle.
- Users can search and filter vehicle and maintenance records.
- The dashboard can display useful fleet maintenance statistics.
- The system can provide reminders for upcoming maintenance.
- The application should work reliably without major errors.
- The application should be accessible through a public URL by Day 41, as required by the capstone plan.
- The project should maintain a clean and organized GitHub repository.
- The project should maintain regular and meaningful GitHub commits throughout development.
- The system should follow proper backend architecture and database practices.
- The smart maintenance enhancement should provide useful predictions or recommendations based on available vehicle maintenance data.

